{
	"name": "Awakened Teapot",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/commodities/treasure/brass-lamp-yellow.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Resembling a ceramic or glass teapot with four legs and decorative flourishes that resemble eyes and a mouth, awakened teapots are actually small constructs that can be found in teahouses and the homes of wealthy nobility, where they are often found lounging on tabletops or in cabinets nested upon lace doilies. When summoned, they approach and patiently wait to be filled with water and tea leaves. It takes an awakened teapot 1 minute to boil water, and another minute for it to steep any tea that it is given. While it is brewing, an awakened teapot cannot move, as all of its energy is diverted to warming the water. Any liquid stored within an awakened teapot is kept warm for up to 6 hours, at which point the construct pours it out.</p><p>Though most are reluctant to part with them, awakened teapots can sometimes be found for sale in cosmopolitan areas for 150 gp.</p>",
